                                        "content":  "Of course! The \"Hello, World!\" program is the traditional first program you write when learning a new language. It simply prints the text \"Hello, World!\" to the console.\n\nHere are examples in some of the most popular programming languages.\n\n### Python (Recommended for beginners)\n\nPython is known for its simple, readable syntax.\n\n```python\n# This line prints the text \"Hello, World!\" to the screen\nprint(\"Hello, World!\")\n```\n\n**How to run it:**\n1.  Save the code in a file named `hello.py`.\n2.  Open a terminal or command prompt.\n3.  Run the file with the command: `python hello.py`\n\n---\n\n### JavaScript\n\nJavaScript is the language of the web. You can run it in two ways:\n\n#### 1. In a web browser (HTML file)\nThis is the most common way. You create an HTML file and add the script inside.\n\n```html\n\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\n\u003chtml\u003e\n\u003chead\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eMy First Program\u003c/title\u003e\n\u003c/head\u003e\n\u003cbody\u003e\n    \u003ch1\u003eCheck the console!\u003c/h1\u003e\n    \u003cscript\u003e\n        // This line prints the text to the browser\u0027s developer console\n        console.log(\"Hello, World!\");\n    \u003c/script\u003e\n\u003c/body\u003e\n\u003c/html\u003e\n```\n**How to run it:**\n1.  Save the code as `index.html`.\n2.  Open the file in any web browser (like Chrome or Firefox).\n3.  Right-click the page and select \"Inspect\" to open the developer tools, then click on the \"Console\" tab to see the output.\n\n#### 2. Using Node.js (on your computer)\nIf you have Node.js installed, you can run it directly from your terminal.\n\n```javascript\n// This line prints the text to the terminal\nconsole.log(\"Hello, World!\");\n```\n**How to run it:**\n1.  Save the code in a file named `hello.js`.\n2.  Open a terminal or command prompt.\n3.  Run the file with the command: `node hello.js`\n\n---\n\n### Java\n\nJava is a strongly-typed, object-oriented language often used in large-scale applications.\n\n```java\n// This is the main class that contains the program\npublic class HelloWorld {\n\n    // This is the main method, the entry point of the program\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        // This line prints the text to the console\n        System.out.println(\"Hello, World!\");\n    }\n}\n```\n**How to run it:**\n1.  Save the code in a file named `HelloWorld.java`.\n2.  Open a terminal or command prompt.\n3.  Compile the code with: `javac HelloWorld.java`\n4.  Run the compiled code with: `java HelloWorld`\n\n---\n\n### C++\n\nC++ is a powerful, compiled language used for system software and game development.\n\n```cpp\n#include \u003ciostream\u003e // This line includes the library for input/output operations\n\n// The main function is the entry point of the program\nint main() {\n    // This line prints the text to the console\n    std::cout \u003c\u003c \"Hello, World!\" \u003c\u003c std::endl;\n    return 0; // Indicates the program finished successfully\n}\n```\n**How to run it:**\n1.  Save the code in a file named `hello.cpp`.\n2.  You need a C++ compiler (like g++).\n3.  Open a terminal or command prompt.\n4.  Compile the code with: `g++ hello.cpp -o hello`\n5.  Run the compiled program with: `./hello`\n\n---\n\n### C#\n\nC# is a modern, object-oriented language from Microsoft, often used with the .NET framework.\n\n```csharp\n// This line includes the library for console input/output\nusing System;\n\n// The main class that contains the program\npublic class Program\n{\n    // The Main method is the entry point of the program\n    public static void Main()\n    {\n        // This line prints the text to the console\n        Console.WriteLine(\"Hello, World!\");\n    }\n}\n```\n**How to run it:**\n1.  You need the .NET SDK installed.\n2.  Save the code in a file named `Program.cs`.\n3.  Open a terminal or command prompt.\n4.  Run the code with: `dotnet run` (make sure you are in the same directory as the file).\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Language    | Code                                      | How to Run                                  |\n|-------------|-------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|\n| **Python**  | `print(\"Hello, World!\")`                  | `python hello.py`                           |\n| **JS (Node)**| `console.log(\"Hello, World!\");`            | `node hello.js`                             |\n| **Java**    | `System.out.println(\"Hello, World!\");`     | `javac HelloWorld.java` then `java HelloWorld` |\n| **C++**     | `std::cout \u003c\u003c \"Hello, World!\" \u003c\u003c std::endl;` | `g++ hello.cpp -o hello` then `./hello` |\n| **C#**      | `Console.WriteLine(\"Hello, World!\");`      | `dotnet run`                                |",
